WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.764 --> 00:00:10.947
The Pop-Song Crew's leadership committee was finishing up their monthly meeting.

2
00:00:12.007 --> 00:00:14.207
The Pop-Song Crew was the school singing club.

3
00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:16.628
"Is there anything else to discuss?"

4
00:00:17.028 --> 00:00:18.689
Jerry, the club's president, asked.

5
00:00:18.709 --> 00:00:22.150
"No," Lucy, the treasurer, replied.

6
00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:25.231
Kathy, the secretary, shook her head.

7
00:00:25.251 --> 00:00:27.891
"Yes!" Mrs.

8
00:00:27.951 --> 00:00:30.112
Mayer, the club's faculty advisor, said eagerly.

9
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.280
She was looking at her phone.

10
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:37.262
"We've been invited to sing at the Newtown Spring Festival next month."

11
00:00:38.022 --> 00:00:39.002
The kids cheered.

12
00:00:40.703 --> 00:00:45.324
"I can't wait to tell the rest of the club members," Jerry said.

13
00:00:45.344 --> 00:00:47.845
"Wait," Lucy said.

14
00:00:47.865 --> 00:00:50.645
"Newtown is three hours away.

15
00:00:51.425 --> 00:00:53.206
We'd have to rent a van to get there."

16
00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:56.707
"How much did it cost last time we rented a van?"

17
00:00:57.047 --> 00:00:58.127
Mrs. Mayer asked.

18
00:00:58.988 --> 00:01:00.448
Lucy checked the club's account.

19
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.821
"Three hundred dollars.

20
00:01:03.281 --> 00:01:05.262
Plus $35 for gas.

21
00:01:05.902 --> 00:01:08.203
We only have twenty dollars left in our account."

22
00:01:09.084 --> 00:01:10.444
She did a quick calculation.

23
00:01:10.464 --> 00:01:13.666
"We'd have to raise $315."

24
00:01:14.526 --> 00:01:15.446
Kathy groaned.

25
00:01:16.727 --> 00:01:21.049
"We can ask everyone in the club to pitch in," Jerry suggested.

26
00:01:22.049 --> 00:01:24.951
Lucy punched the numbers into the calculator app on her phone.

27
00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:30.905
"With 11 members, everyone would have to pay $28.63 each."

28
00:01:30.925 --> 00:01:34.606
"That's a lot for some members," Mrs.

29
00:01:34.666 --> 00:01:35.306
Mayer said.

30
00:01:35.326 --> 00:01:38.827
"Especially since we've had many expenses this year."

31
00:01:38.847 --> 00:01:43.309
"We could hold a fundraiser," Kathy suggested.

32
00:01:43.329 --> 00:01:46.009
"Great idea," Jerry said.

33
00:01:46.029 --> 00:01:47.650
"How about a car wash?"

34
00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:51.831
"Math Club had one last week," Lucy said.

35
00:01:51.851 --> 00:01:54.072
"A bake sale?"

36
00:01:54.312 --> 00:01:55.092
Kathy asked.

37
00:01:56.376 --> 00:02:00.779
"We'd have to sell a lot of cookies to raise $315."

38
00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:01.880
Lucy sighed.

39
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:05.663
"Can we text about this later?"

40
00:02:06.003 --> 00:02:06.784
Kathy asked.

41
00:02:06.804 --> 00:02:09.986
"I'm late for a friend's birthday party at the bowling alley."

42
00:02:10.006 --> 00:02:14.810
"Hey! Science Club did a bowling fundraiser last year," Jerry said.

43
00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:17.011
"They raised a lot of money."

44
00:02:17.031 --> 00:02:20.314
"I'll call and find out the costs," Lucy said.

45
00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:22.896
"Then we can figure out a budget."

46
00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:26.710
The next day Lucy sent a group text to the committee.

47
00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.230
"Bad news.

48
00:02:28.851 --> 00:02:32.993
The bowling alley costs two hundred dollars to rent for two hours.

49
00:02:33.793 --> 00:02:37.335
That means we'd have to raise $515 total."

50
00:02:37.355 --> 00:02:38.536
"Now what?"

51
00:02:38.976 --> 00:02:40.057
Jerry texted back.

52
00:02:40.997 --> 00:02:42.878
Lucy sent a shrugging emoticon.

53
00:02:43.979 --> 00:02:45.760
Ten minutes later Kathy texted.

54
00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.981
"Can you meet me at the bowling alley?

55
00:02:48.721 --> 00:02:49.922
I think I have a solution!"

56
00:02:51.143 --> 00:02:55.757
When Lucy and Jerry arrived at the bowling alley, Kathy introduced them to her friend Carl.

57
00:02:55.777 --> 00:02:58.737
"I'm a big fan of your club!"

58
00:02:58.998 --> 00:02:59.658
Carl said.

59
00:02:59.678 --> 00:03:02.238
"My uncle owns this bowling alley.

60
00:03:03.059 --> 00:03:05.880
He said he'd only charge you one hundred dollars for three hours.

61
00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.340
And the rental fee includes the games and shoe rentals.

62
00:03:10.281 --> 00:03:12.902
He thinks this would be great publicity for the bowling alley."

63
00:03:12.922 --> 00:03:15.922
"That means we'd need to raise $415 total," Lucy said.

64
00:03:15.942 --> 00:03:24.894
"If we charge $10 per person, we'll need at least 42 people to come to our fundraiser."

65
00:03:24.914 --> 00:03:28.937
"What if all eleven club members bring three people with them?"

66
00:03:29.277 --> 00:03:30.218
Jerry suggested.

67
00:03:30.238 --> 00:03:33.440
"That's 44 people," Kathy said.

68
00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.502
"We'd raise $440!"

69
00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:37.562
Lucy said.

70
00:03:37.582 --> 00:03:39.524
"That's more than enough!"

71
00:03:39.544 --> 00:03:42.426
"This is great, Carl," Jerry said.

72
00:03:42.446 --> 00:03:43.627
"Thank you!"

73
00:03:44.507 --> 00:03:47.449
Two weeks later Lucy, Kathy, Jerry, and Mrs.

74
00:03:47.509 --> 00:03:49.590
Mayer sat at a table in the bowling alley.

75
00:03:49.831 --> 00:03:51.552
The fundraiser had been a lot of fun.

76
00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.942
Even more people had shown up than they had expected.

77
00:03:54.962 --> 00:03:56.864
"How much did we make?"

78
00:03:57.284 --> 00:03:58.065
Kathy asked.

79
00:03:59.025 --> 00:04:00.467
Lucy finished counting the money.

80
00:04:00.487 --> 00:04:02.468
"We made $560.

81
00:04:02.488 --> 00:04:05.951
After we pay $100 to the bowling alley, we have a profit of $460.

82
00:04:05.971 --> 00:04:09.534
That covers the costs of the van and gas, and we'll have $125 left over."

83
00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:12.096
"Plus, the twenty dollars in our account," Mrs.

84
00:04:12.136 --> 00:04:12.496
Mayer said.

85
00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.543
"We can buy lunch for everyone on the trip."

86
00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:26.065
Jerry smiled.

87
00:04:26.085 --> 00:04:31.051
"Thanks to Carl and his uncle, The Pop-Song Crew is going to Newtown!"
